Exploration and possession contracts (@ws-contract-exploration: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @workspace-contracts, #requires @ws-exploration, #requires @ws-possession) { r_4CEKJ3R4N8THMQK22APJBYWQ5W
Status: Pending. Owner refinement, 2026-11-14: explore through the things in the workspace and possess an object to move as it, for placement or play.

[Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) owns scheduling. [Exploration](../features/Exploration.lingua) owns EXP.T01–EXP.T05; [Possession](../features/Possession.lingua) owns POS.T01–POS.T06. This Record joins their complete core workflows. [Automatic exploration](../features/Automatic-Exploration.lingua) owns AUTO.T01–AUTO.T03 and AUTO.W01 as an optional extension, outside this core gate.

## Purpose and scope

[Everything's creator](https://blog.playstation.com/?p=189649) describes becoming different things, moving between scales and configurable automatic play. Workspace adopts the consistent object-centered interaction while preserving its authored source, physical units and explicitly selected behavior. Art style, playful animation and scene contents are configurations; they do not require a separate world model or scientific runtime.

The core native flow is: select an object → Observe/Follow or Possess → move through supported controls → release or return. Enter/Surroundings/Back traverse available structure and context. An ordinary object needs no character skeleton. Capabilities come from actual supported profiles; viewing a scientific result does not make its source controllable, and a generic authored motion profile does not establish physical accuracy.

## Milestones

- [ ] **EXP.M01.** Adopt a noncharacter object's viewpoint or frame, follow it and return without changing accepted source, physical dimensions, controller ownership or model settings.
- [ ] **EXP.M02.** Enter available internals or a linked model, move outward and return along the actual entry path across scales, including a reused occurrence and a missing/unavailable target. The current subject, frame, units and relationship remain understandable.
- [ ] **EXP.M03.** Possess one occurrence to place it with ordinary movement/turning, numeric/snapped correction, validated acceptance, one undo and save/reopen. Unselected copies and shared source remain unchanged.
- [ ] **EXP.M04.** Possess an object to play in a bounded temporary activity; discard the trial or explicitly Keep pose through the accepted edit path. Trial motion/events never silently alter accepted geometry, commitments or external systems.
- [ ] **EXP.M05.** Switch/release control reliably under focus, permission, source and support changes; preserve one active state writer, separate camera/object input, declared behavior fidelity and bounded cost.

## Interaction, state and authority

- [ ] **EXP.R01.** Separate the participant, observed subject, possessed occurrence, camera anchor, selected behavior model and active control owner. Store only needed stable references and preferences in the existing paths. A camera-relative presentation or a local magnified view does not change placement, speed units, mass, simulated time or physics fidelity. Observe remains usable for a permitted object whose control is unsupported.
- [ ] **EXP.R02.** Use declared source relationships for physical components and explicit bindings for linked models/specimens. Entering a lamp's available PCB may inspect its real design; opening a representative material specimen is visibly a linked sample, not a claim to enumerate that lamp's atoms. No missing level is invented and no fixed molecule-to-galaxy ladder belongs in the engine. Bounded navigation history stores the actual occurrence path and view context, not every intermediate mesh or another source copy.
- [ ] **EXP.R03.** Movement profiles state local axes, units, support and allowed actions, with an authored generic option for ordinary objects. Camera placement/inspection and object translation/rotation are independently routed. Mount/Sand typing never becomes held movement. Constraint, attachment, port and source-validity rules still govern placement; explicit unsupported status is preferable to detaching or modifying another subsystem implicitly.
- [ ] **EXP.R04.** Place previews captured-revision edits and accepts the exact validated final pose once through normal undo/save. Apply or ready editor-exit adoption follows the existing edit protocol; Cancel and failed/stale adoption preserve current accepted state. Play uses isolated temporary activity state over captured sources, with visible scope and existing resource admission. Default trial signals affect only that scope. Keep pose is an explicit new validated placement edit, not a rewind or adoption of the trial's complete event history.
- [ ] **EXP.R05.** Acquiring control uses existing activity authority and supported intent channels. Neither possessing nor changing camera distance upgrades grants, selects a new physics model, starts microscopic simulation or changes solver accuracy. A run already governed by a numerical or character controller accepts possession only through its supported ownership/input transition. A local trial cannot share an output writer with the live source. Revoke, focus loss, held-input target switch and stale generations stop old input before a new owner starts.
- [ ] **EXP.R06.** Keep one simple native action and familiar controls, with visible Place/Play and a recoverable exit. Use existing selection/tree/inspector, focus, transaction and accessibility families. Preserve the [Lince edit-panel geometry requirement](../../Lince.lingua): the panel's placement/height and visible bottom-left workspace controls continue to work. Reduced motion and an immediate transition option remain usable. Missing/private/offline contents show a usable permitted context rather than a trapped camera or fabricated successful entry.
- [ ] **EXP.R07.** Model history/source identity remains stable across visual simplification, scene magnification and context changes. Inactive visited detail releases after its last real lease; active control and causal dependencies retain their separately admitted demand. Save document/profile choices and view preferences through existing services. Crash/reopen restores accepted source and valid view state without replaying transient play events, reacquiring control or resuming held input.

## Ordered integration and acceptance

Exploration first proves its independent observation/traversal export on supplied objects. Possession joins that export with real functional activity/authority and geometry acceptance. Each package completes its own ordered tasks before this contract runs the combined workflows. Core acceptance then replays the same behavior beside the other Workspace features. Optional automatic exploration and later physical/rig adapters have separate completion evidence and do not delay the base authored flow.

| Workflow | Task and milestone coverage | Required native evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **EXP.W01 — See from a thing** | EXP.T01/EXP.T02/EXP.T04/EXP.T05; EXP.M01 | Select a box, lamp-shaped object and changing reference frame from both scene and list; Observe/Follow and return. Correct occurrence/anchor/frame and separate input; accepted transforms/model choices/control grants unchanged. Review camera usability and exit discoverability. |
| **EXP.W02 — Enter, leave and find the way back** | EXP.T01/EXP.T03–EXP.T05; EXP.M02 | Traverse nested parts and an explicitly linked representative specimen; Back restores the entry context, including a reused definition under a different parent. Test a root without outer context, deleted/rebound target, missing/private/offline detail and unit/origin changes. Verify dimensions, identity, permitted context and bounded history/residency. |
| **EXP.W03 — Move into position as the object** | POS.T01/POS.T02/POS.T05/POS.T06; EXP.M03 | Possess one copy, move/turn, make a numeric/snapped correction, Apply or ready exit, undo and reopen. Compare exact final pose/receipts against intended input; one accepted edit, no shared-definition/unselected-copy mutation. Cancel, constraint conflict and stale source preserve accepted state. |
| **EXP.W04 — Play, discard or keep a pose** | POS.T01/POS.T03/POS.T05/POS.T06; EXP.M04 | Move in an authored free profile and a supported surface profile. Stop restores current accepted source; Keep pose produces only the validated selected pose edit and supports undo. Exercise a neighboring functional device and prove trial events do not reach the live graph or operational records. |
| **EXP.W05 — Release and transfer control** | POS.T04–POS.T06; EXP.M05 | Switch targets while a key is held, type into mounted content, lose support/focus/permission, disconnect and deliver stale input. Stop old intent, preserve one state owner, retain valid sources and release session demand. A visitor can observe while unauthorized possession is unavailable. |

- [ ] **EXP.P01.** Pin EXP.F01 source/build/profile and adopt the applicable B25/B38/B31/B42 input/frame/preview/admission limits before implementation. Add bounded context/possession counters and invariants to the existing native suites where those boundaries are exercised. Use independent expected transforms, captured revision/receipt assertions, controlled late completions and source snapshots; a camera-only animation cannot prove possession or accepted placement.
- [ ] **EXP.P02.** Run EXP.W01–EXP.W05 through the real native/backend/view/activity/persistence paths, including local/offline and supported hosted cases. Review subject/path readability, relative movement, sense of scale, camera comfort, Place/Play distinction and recovery. Record transition/preview age, input/frame percentiles, CPU/active and retained bytes, queue peaks and last-demand release. Isolate timing from concurrent builds; absent counters stay unmeasured.
- [ ] **EXP.P03.** Repeat view changes with the same behavior selected, then reduce visual detail while moving. Show that physical dimensions, authority, model choice and requested observables are retained. Publish each supported control profile's actual semantics and unsupported cases. Full core acceptance consumes this evidence plus its mixed-workload replay; optional tour and unbuilt numerical/character adapters remain explicitly separate.

## Bounded fixture and optional extensions

**EXP.F01** extends the supplied local B38/B42 scene: two occurrences sharing a simple source; an unrigged box/lamp-shaped object; ready ground and an opening; nested reusable parts; a changing frame; an explicitly linked representative specimen view; a mounted input surface; and a nearby functional lamp/sensor. Use actual existing sources/operators and source/license metadata. Observation can use supplied static structure and controlled accepted frame updates before functional evaluation exists; the possession join adds the real B42 activity. Start with a 32-entry history and a 16-target optional tour as bounded test configurations, not universal product limits. Adopt other counts, precision and resource thresholds from the existing measured profiles. No anatomical atlas, physical material population, globe or rig editor is fixture setup.

**AUTO.W01 — Optional observation tour.** Owned by [Automatic exploration](../features/Automatic-Exploration.lingua). Start explicitly, visit configured subjects/scales and supported activity observations, interrupt during loading/transition and return. Preserve read-only behavior, manual priority, selected clocks/model settings and resource/network limits; stopping settles to ordinary idle. No unattended scene editing, possession, continuous model-provider loop or new simulation is implied. The optional feature remains pending without blocking EXP.M01–EXP.M05.

**Later provider integration.** [Character motion](../features/Character-Motion.lingua), [rigid dynamics](../features/Rigid.lingua) and [physical articulation](../features/Physical-Articulation.lingua) supply their own supported intent/state interfaces. A possession integration claim for one of these requires both verified providers and a scoped EXP.W05 replay proving ownership, release and model-specific state continuity. Missing adapters stay unavailable; their tests do not silently become prerequisites for ordinary box/lamp placement or authored play.

**Fantasy worlds within worlds.** A mounted/linked view can already present another model at an arbitrary display scale. Traversable impossible portals, recursive world generation and crossing a physical body between unrelated worlds remain deferred ideas; this refinement adds no such implementation or acceptance gate. Camera traversal through explicitly available structure does not assert physical containment of every linked model.

## Completion and retained handoff

Mark this contract complete only after EXP.M01–EXP.M05 and EXP.W01–EXP.W05 pass with actual source/build, bounded profile, native evidence and measured results. Retain operation/profile ownership, Place/Play/Keep pose acceptance and recovery semantics, context/history limits and unresolved adapters. Current outcome: planning only; no exploration or possession implementation is claimed.
